Scott,

Thanks for the feedback. You are correct, the default behavior of deployApp() is to attempt to replicate the current environment as closely as possible, with the goal being that the output of runApp() and deployApp() are as similar as possible. However, we are interested in allowing to have more control over their application dependencies, probably with some type of integration with the new packrat package <https://github.com/rstudio/packrat>. It would be great if you could explain more of the use case you are envisioning where being about to specify application dependencies manually would be helpful.

Thanks,
-Andy

